  "outcome": "Failure. While functionally correct and maintaining high occupancy, the blockwise approach is slower than the baseline fused per-row kernel, due to redundant loads and reductions. No new correctness or masking bugs are present, but the performance goal is not met.",
  "next_step": "Revert to the single-pass per-row fused kernel, which performs all reductions in one load pass for N <= BLOCK. For wider rows (very large N), a blockwise reduction may become necessary, but for the current case (N=781 < BLOCK=1024), it is strictly suboptimal. No further changes required for this shape and hardware; tuning BLOCK or num_warps may be explored for larger N."
}

